  "executive_briefing": "The 2026 global tax landscape is defined by the rigid consolidation of the OECD Pillar Two 15% minimum tax, which is now moving from conceptual framework to active enforcement across major jurisdictions. Nations, particularly in the ASEAN region, are recalibrating their corporate tax incentives\u2014balancing statutory rates like Singapore\u2019s 17% with complex Domestic Top-up Tax regimes\u2014to maintain FDI appeal while adhering to global standards. Simultaneously, digital tax administration is accelerating via mandatory e-invoicing, with Singapore\u2019s InvoiceNow serving as a benchmark. Geopolitical trade volatility remains a persistent feature, as major economies continue to leverage tariffs as primary instruments of industrial and national economic strategy.",
